# Coding Conventions

Full technical vision: `docs/vision.md`.

## Principles

- **KISS**: implement only what is needed to validate the idea. No over-engineering.
- **Functional style**: no classes, no OOP. Use plain functions and modules.
- **Async everywhere**: all I/O (Telegram, LLM) must be `async/await`.

## Module Responsibilities

Each module has one responsibility. Do not mix concerns across modules:

- `src/main.py` — wires components, starts polling only.
- `src/config.py` — loads and validates env. Fail fast if required vars are missing.
- `src/handlers.py` — Telegram message handlers only.
- `src/llm.py` — one public async function to call the LLM. No Telegram logic here.
- `src/dialog_store.py` — in-memory `dict[int, list[dict]]` keyed by `chat_id`. No I/O.

## Configuration

- All config comes from `.env`. No hardcoded secrets or values.
- Required vars: `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `LLM_PROVIDER`, `LLM_BASE_URL`, `LLM_API_KEY`, `LLM_MODEL`, `SYSTEM_PROMPT`.
- `SYSTEM_PROMPT` is mandatory — the app must not start without it.

## Logging

- Use stdlib `logging` only. No third-party logging libs.
- Log to `stdout`. Format: `time | level | module | message`.
- Never log secrets or full user message content.

## Error Handling

- On LLM/network error: send a short user-facing message, log the technical reason at `ERROR` level.
